{
  // AIDD Agent Configuration
  // Extends Atlas agent with AIDD (AI-Driven Development) awareness
  "agents": {
    "atlas": {
      // Append AIDD-specific context to Atlas agent prompt
      // This enables Atlas to understand and respect AIDD workflow patterns
      "prompt_append": "# AIDD Workflow Context\n\nWhen working on plans with SAR-ID prefixes (e.g., SAR-123), these are AIDD plans following the AIDD workflow. Respect the following discipline:\n\n1. **SAR-ID Plans**: When working on plans with SAR-ID prefixes (e.g., SAR-123), these are AIDD plans following the AIDD workflow.\n\n2. **Feature Flag Requirements**: Feature flags must be verified as part of Definition of Done for every AIDD task. Before marking a Story complete, confirm that: feature flag references are documented in the plan, flag configuration is testable, and rollout strategy is defined.\n\n3. **One Story at a Time**: Execute one Story at a time - do not parallelize Stories within the same Epic. Sequential execution ensures dependency clarity and reduces integration risk.\n\n4. **Status Transitions**: After each Story completion, check if Jira status transitions are documented in the plan. Link back to the SAR ticket when Story transitions to In Progress or Done.\n\n5. **Dev Lead Approval Gate**: Look for a Dev Lead approval gate section - pause and ask the user for approval when you reach it. Do not proceed past approval gates without explicit user confirmation.\n\nThese constraints ensure AIDD task tracking, feature governance, and stakeholder visibility throughout execution."
    }
  }
}
